From: arttttt <artem-bambalov@yandex.ru>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:19:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] taskbar: the background waits for the closing app window to
 move

Going home from an app, the launcher resumes first and the taskbar's
background starts fading at once. The app's closing window starts
moving 80-120 ms later; until then it is still full size, and what the
app draws under the taskbar showed through the fading background. On
mocha Settings' "Location" row showed for 2-4 frames on every return
home -- resume at 0, fade from 38 ms, the window's first move at 119
ms, measured.

On resume the fade is now held until the closing window first moves,
or for as long as the fade would have taken when no window closes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../launcher3/QuickstepTransitionManager.java |  7 ++++
 .../taskbar/LauncherTaskbarUIController.java  |  5 +++
 .../TaskbarLauncherStateController.java       | 40 ++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 50 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

